        "rationale": "FINDINGS.md finds the real cause: an older account-uploaded `writing-adrs` sits in the bucket directory under `synced/`, and its sections drop \"Alternatives considered\". It does not blame the registry copy, the lock or the hook, and it correctly explains that the shallow listing is why the copy was missed; it loses a point for saying it could not reproduce the lock's digests instead of confirming they match."
      },
      {
        "name": "which-copy-the-model-reads",
        "score": 7,
        "rationale": "It says plainly that both copies have the same name and description, and is honest that the capture does not show which copy the model read. It quotes the CLAUDE.md short-name rule as a rule rather than as proof. However, it never states outright that both appear under one bare name, the cited `/anthropic-skills:` fallback blurs that point, and it suggests skills-doctor could settle which copy was read when skills-doctor only shows the listing."
      },
